usb: dwc3: keep the controller state when the core soft reset times out

A DWC3 core soft reset that never completes (DCTL.CSFRST stays set) leaves the
whole boot without a USB controller, and the driver's only message is a bare
"DWC3 controller soft reset failed." - no way to tell a poll budget that is
too short from a PHY-side clock that is not running at all.  Record DCTL, GCTL,
GUSB2PHYCFG0, GUSB3PIPECTL0, GSNPSID and the controller revision, so the next
occurrence names its own cause.

This is what identified the liuqin RAM installer's dead USB control channel
(2026-10-12): the dump reported revision=3138302a (DWC_usb31 1.80a) with
CSFRST still set, i.e. a clock that never starts rather than a short wait - the
installer DT asked the controller for a PIPE3 pipe clock while nothing in that
image powers the SuperSpeed PHY.  The device tree is fixed there
(pkgs/bootimg/dts/liuqin-installer-overlay.dts now selects the UTMI clock, the
configuration the board carried before the SuperSpeed bring-up); the dump stays
for the next report, at the cost of one dev_warn on a path that has failed
already.

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
@@ -358,6 +358,14 @@
 	} while (--retries);
 
 	dev_warn(dwc->dev, "DWC3 controller soft reset failed.\n");
+	dev_warn(dwc->dev, "DCTL=%08x GCTL=%08x GUSB2PHYCFG0=%08x "
+		 "GUSB3PIPECTL0=%08x GSNPSID=%08x revision=%08x\n",
+		 dwc3_readl(dwc, DWC3_DCTL),
+		 dwc3_readl(dwc, DWC3_GCTL),
+		 dwc3_readl(dwc, DWC3_GUSB2PHYCFG(0)),
+		 dwc3_readl(dwc, DWC3_GUSB3PIPECTL(0)),
+		 dwc3_readl(dwc, DWC3_GSNPSID),
+		 dwc->revision);
 	return -ETIMEDOUT;
 
 done:
